WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:01.080 --> 00:03.180
Let's look at AVEC in action.

2
00:03.240 --> 00:05.500
Meet Svea and her colleague Bo.

3
00:05.560 --> 00:07.980
They've worked together for almost five years,

4
00:08.040 --> 00:13.660
but at times they struggle to maintain
a positive and productive relationship at work.

5
00:14.120 --> 00:17.020
Bo sometimes has difficulty listening to Svea.

6
00:17.080 --> 00:19.260
He has a habit of letting his mind wander,

7
00:19.320 --> 00:25.980
and when he suddenly thinks of a great idea, he tends to blurt it out,
unintentionally interrupting her.

8
00:26.040 --> 00:28.860
At times Bo's behavior irritates Svea.

9
00:28.920 --> 00:35.260
She wonders if he only cares about his own ideas and opinions,
since he often fails to listen to hers.

10
00:35.320 --> 00:42.447
Once in a meeting he interrupted her,
then suggested a new idea she had shared with him only the day before.

11
00:42.507 --> 00:45.167
Bo was totally unaware he had done it.

12
00:45.227 --> 00:51.167
Svea finds that she's often not very excited to work with Bo
and prefers to work with others.

13
00:51.227 --> 00:54.207
For her part, Svea can be quick to judgment.

14
00:54.267 --> 00:58.847
While she rarely says anything explicitly to Bo,
her annoyance shows.

15
00:58.907 --> 01:04.367
Bo suspects her cross looks are often directed at him,
though he's never asked her about it.

16
01:04.427 --> 01:09.327
But Bo thinks Svea is judging his ideas or his style, or both.

17
01:09.387 --> 01:11.807
Or perhaps she simply doesn't like him.

18
01:11.867 --> 01:17.087
The reality is that most of the time,
she's merely annoyed that he doesn't seem to listen.

19
01:17.147 --> 01:19.967
Bo has started disengaging during these interactions,

20
01:20.027 --> 01:24.586
and Svea finds herself jumping in and interrupting Bo
when he does speak.

21
01:24.646 --> 01:30.266
Over time their strained relationship has started
to affect their productivity and effectiveness.

22
01:30.406 --> 01:36.906
What if each of them could approach this with more attention,
vulnerability, empathy and compassion?

23
01:38.646 --> 01:44.266
Imagine Bo actively listening to Svea's point of view
and asking more questions.

24
01:44.326 --> 01:50.826
And what if, instead of keeping her emotions to herself,
Svea shared her feelings directly and openly?

25
01:50.886 --> 01:59.306
What if that, in turn, helped each of them to put themselves in each other's shoes
and to genuinely commit to helping one another?

26
01:59.606 --> 02:02.346
AVEC helps us build interpersonal resilience,

27
02:02.406 --> 02:12.086
and it makes the difference between a relationship being the thing that helps you overcome challenges
versus the relationship actually being the challenge.
